<statement>
<p>
	This function returns the state structure containing the game data and information.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>grid_size</pf> (1 x 1) integer — positive integer spaces on one side of the grid</p>
			<p><pf>difficulty</pf> (1 x k) number — char array containing one of the three difficulty levels: <pf>'easy'</pf>, <pf>'normal'</pf>, or <pf>'hard'</pf>.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>state</pf> (1 x 1) number — struct object containing the default game state.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>We coded this in class together.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>The only thing you need to do is choose you setting values.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>This function should call both (1)</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>random_jerk_generator</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>, and (2)</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>compute_data_matrix</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
